Jove <invalid@invalid.invalid> writes:

>   Here are some tips for the movement key configuration.
>   'j' goes down because it descends below the line.
>   'k' goes up because it extends upward.
>   'h' goes to the left because it's to the left.
>   'l' goes to the right because it's to the right.

Some movement keys are also related to ASCII control codes:

Ascii code 8, ctrl-h, is the backspace code that moves cursor left, just
like h in Nethack.
Ascii code 10, ctrl-j, is linefeed, moves cursor down like j in Nethack.

